"### F. Auto-Refresh Loop with Lifecycle Awareness
```java
@Override
protected void onResume() {
    super.onResume();
    autoRefreshHandler.postDelayed(autoRefreshRunnable, 3000);
}

@Override
protected void onPause() {
    super.onPause();
    autoRefreshHandler.removeCallbacks(autoRefreshRunnable);
}
```
*Critical Best Practice*: If the user switches apps or locks their screen, `onPause()` is invoked. By removing scheduled callbacks in `onPause()`, we prevent background battery drain and memory leaks.

### G. Floating Gaming Overlay HUD (`OverlayService`)
```java
WindowManager.LayoutParams params = new WindowManager.LayoutParams(
    WindowManager.LayoutParams.WRAP_CONTENT,
    WindowManager.LayoutParams.WRAP_CONTENT,
    WindowManager.LayoutParams.TYPE_APPLICATION_OVERLAY,
    WindowManager.LayoutParams.FLAG_NOT_FOCUSABLE,
    PixelFormat.TRANSLUCENT
);
windowManager.addView(overlayView, params);
```
- **`TYPE_APPLICATION_OVERLAY`**: Tells Android to render this window on top of all other running applications and full-screen games.
- **`FLAG_NOT_FOCUSABLE`**: Critical for games! Touches outside our HUD pass directly into the game controls so gameplay is never blocked.
- **Fluid Dragging Math**: Using `MotionEvent.ACTION_MOVE` and `(event.getRawX() - initialTouchX)`, the HUD repositions dynamically wherever the gamer slides their finger.
- **Foreground Service**: Ensures the Android OS does not terminate the monitoring loop when the device is under heavy CPU/GPU load from 3D gaming.

---

## 5. Future Upgrade Roadmap"

