"### H. Real-Time FPS Counter (`FpsMonitor` via `Choreographer`)
```java
Choreographer.getInstance().postFrameCallback(new Choreographer.FrameCallback() {
    @Override
    public void doFrame(long frameTimeNanos) {
        frameCount++;
        long elapsed = frameTimeNanos - startNanos;
        if (elapsed >= 500_000_000L) { // 500ms sample window
            int fps = (int) ((frameCount * 1_000_000_000L) / elapsed);
            listener.onFpsUpdated(fps);
            frameCount = 0;
            startNanos = frameTimeNanos;
        }
        Choreographer.getInstance().postFrameCallback(this);
    }
});
```
- **Hardware VSYNC Coordination**: `Choreographer` is Android's internal pulse coordinator that triggers whenever the display hardware is ready to present a new frame (60Hz, 90Hz, 120Hz, 144Hz).
- **Nanosecond Precision**: We count every single frame callback over a rolling 500ms window, delivering responsive, real-time FPS numbers without jitter.
- **Zero Battery Waste**: Automatically calls `removeFrameCallback()` when the app or overlay is stopped or backgrounded."

